# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@decoricks-cluster0.q4qnwaa.mongodb.net/?appName=Decoricks-Cluster0

# TEST-RUNNER ONLY: remove from dev and prod copies.
# This is a template for a DEV/PROD `.env.local`, so MONGODB_TEST_DB is left
# commented out on purpose. src/lib/db-name.ts REFUSES TO BOOT when it is set
# outside a test runner (NODE_ENV!=test and E2E_TEST_MODE!=1), so an active
# value here would crash the app on the first DB call. The Playwright webServer
# injects it automatically for E2E; you never set it yourself for dev or prod.
# MONGODB_TEST_DB=decoricks_test   # uncomment ONLY for a local test run

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sessions (replaces NextAuth)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs CSRF tokens. Minimum 16 characters.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-32-random-bytes

# Minutes of inactivity before a session expires. Defaults to 7 days; the
# window restarts on each qualifying (non-background) authenticated request.
# Sliding inactivity window: 12 hours. The window restarts on each qualifying
# authenticated request, so an active user is never logged out mid-session.
SESSION_TTL_MINUTES=720
# Absolute ceiling on a session's life, measured from the moment it was created.
# A session may slide for at most 7 days however active the user is. This must
# be greater than or equal to SESSION_TTL_MINUTES; the app refuses to boot on a
# configuration that violates that.
SESSION_MAX_LIFETIME_MINUTES=10080
# Minimum seconds between session slides, so bursts of requests do not cause
# bursts of writes. Auto-polling requests never slide.
SESSION_SLIDE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password policy
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12
BCRYPT_COST=12

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Login lockout
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOGIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
LOGIN_WINDOW_MINUTES=15
LOCKOUT_MINUTES=15

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# First Founder (used only by `npm run seed`)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The seed refuses to run against MONGODB_TEST_DB and will not overwrite an
# existing Founder's credentials on rerun.
FOUNDER_EMAIL=founder@decoricks.pk
FOUNDER_NAME=Abdullah
FOUNDER_PASSWORD=<at least 12 chars, upper+lower+number>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phase 9 Web Push (VAPID) — OPTIONAL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three are optional. Leave them unset and the app still notifies in-app
# (bell + live signal + polling); `deliverPush` is a silent no-op and the
# "Enable notifications" control reports push as not configured. To turn OS-level
# push on (delivered even when the app is closed, and on an installed iOS PWA),
# generate a key pair once and paste the three values:
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys --json
# The public key is client-visible (NEXT_PUBLIC_*); the private key and subject
# stay server-only and are never sent to the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@decoricks.pk
